//? Title: Kangaroo logarithms: actual seeded jumps and exact interval distances
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The native algorithm precomputes a seeded32-entry jump table, walks a complete
tame trail from g^b, then walks the target until a trail lookup supplies a
candidate. Collisions can include cyclic-group aliases, so every candidate is
range-checked and verified by modular powering. Failure after finite attempts
does not show that no logarithm exists, and a five-setting plot does not prove a
square-root work law. Exact widened distances preserve b+distance near the
uint64 limit. The original three secrets and five interval widths remain; no
dataset is needed.

$$ g^{b+d_T}=h g^{d_W},\qquad x=b+d_T-d_W,\qquad a\le x\le b. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pollard_kangaroo_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/pollard_kangaroo.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto target = dm::algorithms::mod_pow(2, 15, 1019);
    auto t = dm::algorithms::pollard_kangaroo_trace(2, target, 1019, 12, 18);
    std::print("\n| actual walk | before | slot | exponent jump | after | exact distance after | actual tame " "trail exponent |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < std::min<std::size_t>(6, t.jumps.size()); ++i) {
        auto &r = t.jumps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   r.wild ? "wild" : "tame", r.before, r.slot, r.step, r.after,
                   dm::algorithms::uint128_text(r.distance_after),
                   dm::algorithms::uint128_text(r.trail_exponent_after));
    }

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual seeded first jump size\n{}", t.table[0].step));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual first tame point update\n{} to{}",
                       t.jumps[0].before, t.jumps[0].after));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual verified run outcome\nfound={}, x={}",
                       t.run.result.found, t.run.result.x));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pollard_kangaroo_tiny.svg");
}
```
