> API and interpretation

Every block is a complete editable C++ program. Reusable searches, walks,
geometry decisions, fixture histories and algorithm work live in the canonical
library. Captured records own their values and are not reconstructed by a second
algorithm in the report. Explicit policies count the documented selected calls,
records or scalar entries; they are not peak-byte or wall-clock budgets.
Original reference curves are labelled as references, and finite returned
results are not promoted into universal convergence, recovery, scaling or speed
guarantees.

Independent integer powers check actual tables and jumps, exact distance/range
decisions and returned equations, including a requested interval next to
UINT64_MAX. Frozen comparisons preserve original ordinary-interval results and
complete jump counts. The shared batch passes83 native regression tests,18
directly instrumented sanitizer tests,84 compiled and executed public
examples,391/391 scoped documentation definitions, standalone and installed
header checks, a linked installed consumer and ten representative symbol hovers.
All four complete programs execute and their computed results and local figures
survive HTML and Markdown export. Build receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-284-293/`.
